From 0018c4f87bb84548e4723fbde8ff195c3c78f147 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 18:04:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(health): one go-live scoreboard for /api/health and pnpm
 doctor

Why
---
The funnel is deployed and has taken zero euros. What stops it is not code:
a Stripe key, three price IDs, a webhook secret, APP_URL and the operator's
own identity. /api/health reported six coarse checks and a two-state verdict
("ok" / "degraded"), so a deployment that could not take a single payment
looked the same as one that could take money but not send a confirmation.
The go-live doctor from 0010 was never applied (scripts/doctor.mjs is absent
from the tree, and 0010 no longer applies to package.json), so there was no
operator checklist at all.

This patch adds one register, shared/health.ts, and makes both consumers read
it:

  * GET /api/health returns the scoreboard: for every capability its id,
    severity, present, cost_if_missing (plain German), fix, the variables
    that feed it, and - when something is set but unusable - a problem that
    describes the defect without quoting the value. Plus a presence map of
    the thirteen documented variables (booleans), stripeMode (live / test /
    null) and a three-state verdict:

      blocked   at least one revenue blocker missing - no euro can move
      degraded  money can move; fulfilment or record-keeping cannot fully
      ok        every revenue blocker and fulfilment capability present

  * pnpm doctor (tsx scripts/doctor.ts [url]) fetches that payload and
    prints it: revenue blockers first with cost and fix, then fulfilment,
    then optional surfaces; the Stripe test-mode caveat and the end-to-end
    verification sequence when payment is configured. Exit 0 = no revenue
    blocker, 1 = revenue blocker, 2 = unreachable or no scoreboard.

Severities:
  revenue_blocker  STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, one price per SKU (read from
                   PILOT_OFFER_SERVER_CONFIG), APP_URL, STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET,
                   shared/legal-entity.ts
  fulfilment       RESEND_API_KEY, RESEND_FROM_EMAIL, LEAD_NOTIFICATION_EMAIL,
                   UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL + _TOKEN, ADMIN_API_TOKEN
  optional         ET_API_KEYS

Usability, not mere presence: a value left as written in .env.example
("sk_test_...") is not configuration; a localhost or plain-http APP_URL is
refused in production; a publishable key in STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, a product id
in a price variable, a half-configured Upstash pair or an admin token below
16 characters (which the admin surface already refuses) are named as
problems. legal_entity is present only when legalEntityPublishable() holds -
the record is checked, not just the flag.

The legacy `failing`, `checks` and `config` fields are kept; `config` is
byte-compatible so smoke-test.sh keeps working. `failing`/`checks` are now
projections of the register (check names are the capability ids).

Invariants preserved
--------------------
  * /api/health tells the truth: missing Stripe is "blocked", never "ok".
  * No secret value leaves the server. Only names, booleans and a derived
    mode. Pinned by a unit test that feeds real-looking secrets and by the
    same pattern e2e/security.spec.ts applies to the live endpoint.
  * HTTP status of /api/health stays 200 in every state (uptime probes).
  * LEGAL_ENTITY stays configured: false; nothing is invented.
  * No statutory paragraph number anywhere; the citation tree scan passes.
  * No Stripe call, no dummy charge, no price ID reaches the client.
  * shared/health.ts is DOM-free and performs no I/O.
  * Webhook, checkout, ledger and lead code untouched.

Tests added
-----------
  client/src/lib/health.test.ts (32 cases): register order and severities;
  one price capability per sellable tier; top-level payload keys and
  per-capability fields pinned; env presence map is exactly the documented
  variables as booleans; ok / degraded / blocked derivation including the
  shipped legal-entity default; .env.example template values, localhost
  APP_URL in production, malformed keys/ids/emails/tokens, half-set Upstash,
  unparseable ET_API_KEYS; stripeMode; no configured value in the report or
  the doctor output; nothing matching the e2e secret pattern; doctor exit
  codes 0 / 1 / 2 including a pre-scoreboard deployment and a report whose
  status and scoreboard disagree (fails closed); doctor output order and
  test-mode caveat.
  e2e/api.spec.ts: the live endpoint returns a valid status, a capability
  list with cost and fix for each entry, and a boolean-only env map.

Not in this patch
-----------------
  * No value for any variable, no legal entity, no domain - operator facts.
  * No change to how APP_URL feeds canonical URLs, sitemap or OG (0020).
  * No check that mail addresses are domain mailboxes rather than freemail.
  * No README update (0041).
  * 0010-go-live-doctor.patch is superseded by this patch and must not be
    applied after it: it would add a second doctor and a stray
    marktlage.html.

